-- =========================================================================
-- hudl -- audit and change capture
--
-- GENERATED by tools/gen_audit.py. Do not edit by hand; edit the generator.
--
-- Three things live here:
--
--   1. updated_at triggers, so the incremental-extraction watermark is
--      maintained by the database rather than trusted to the application.
--      An application-maintained timestamp is missed on exactly the UPDATE
--      paths nobody remembers.
--
--   2. A change log, which is what makes CDC extraction modelable. A
--      high-water-mark read of updated_at cannot observe a deleted row --
--      the row is simply gone -- so deletes are recorded with their prior
--      contents for the lakehouse to tombstone.
--
--   3. Role grants, including the REVOKEs that make the PII satellite split
--      an access control rather than merely a layout.
-- =========================================================================

-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- updated_at maintenance: 19 tables.
-- common.touch_updated_at() is shared by every schema using the default
-- watermark column name.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
